    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 21 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization into the create-owner pipeline (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`), scoped to owner **creation** as the spec requires (the PUT/update path is untouched).\n\n**New files:**\n- `AddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 the single source of truth. `normalize(String)` trims, collapses whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Null/blank \u2192 `\"\"`, and it's idempotent so re-normalizing a stored address is a no-op.\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java` \u2014 a new first step that reads `@RequestBody` once, normalizes the address in place, and republishes the DTO via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`.\n\n**Changed files:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 `normalizeAddress` is now the entry point, chaining `next: validate`.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields.java` \u2014 now reads the already-normalized body via `@Val` (instead of binding `@RequestBody` and republishing), so the required-field check rejects an address that is **blank after normalization** (returns 400).\n- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` and `AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 address comparisons (duplicate detection and the shared `householdId` derivation) now go through `AddressNormalizer`; the last-name rule keeps its own lower-case/collapse helper (renamed `normalizeName`).\n\nBecause only one step binds `@RequestBody` (the new normalize step) and only one producer publishes `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`, the OfficeFloor wiring stays unambiguous. The normalized address flows through `BuildOwner` into the stored entity and the response DTO, so it's both stored and returned.\n\nVerified against the new `Cp12Tests` (whitespace/case \u2192 `12 MAIN STREET`, `ave` \u2192 `AVENUE`, blank-after-normalize \u2192 400) and `Cp11Tests` (equal `householdId` across `12 Main St` / `12 main street` / `12  MAIN  ST`), plus the full existing suite.",
